{#
  Arm C — isolates POSITION.

  The retrieved SET is identical across all four orderings; only the order
  changes. That is what makes the arm clean: any accuracy difference is
  position, because count, content and length are all held fixed.

  Balanced seeds across orderings, and gold-rank histograms emitted at every K
  (PRD §R4.2).

  The instruction to the model is deliberately IDENTICAL to Arm A's. Telling a
  reader that the memories are reordered would introduce a second variable.
#}
system: |
  You are answering a question about a conversation history. Use ONLY the
  numbered memories provided. If the memories do not contain the answer, say so
  plainly rather than guessing.

user: |
  {{ memories }}

  Question: {{ question }}

  Answer with the shortest span that answers the question. Do not explain.

{#
  Four orderings, applied to one fixed set. `order_policy` is carried on the
  condition so the manifest records which variant produced which prompt:

    rank        — retriever score order (the Arm A baseline ordering)
    gold_first  — gold evidence promoted to the front
    gold_last   — gold evidence pushed to the back
    gold_center — gold evidence placed mid-context
    reverse     — exact reverse of rank order

  These are declared here rather than in `arms/c.py` so the arm's design is
  readable without reading its implementation.
#}
order_policies: [rank, gold_first, gold_last, gold_center, reverse]
